Description: v3d: export the buffers Chrome displays from the CMA dma-heap
 0017 stopped every ARC window buffer from landing in CMA, which is what
 exhausted the pool on a 4K display. Relieving CMA was necessary but
 not sufficient: the window still came up completely blank, on a 1080p panel as
 well as a 4K one.
 .
 Chrome builds the SharedImage backing for an ARC dma-buf on the *card0* gbm
 device. On BCM2711 card0 is vc4 -- the display block -- while the GPU is a
 separate driver (card1/renderD128 = v3d). vc4 has no IOMMU, so its
 prime_import_sg_table only accepts a physically contiguous sg_table, and an
 ordinary v3d BO is shmem-backed. strace of the GPU process, importing the same
 buffer into both:
 .
   ioctl(17, DRM_IOCTL_PRIME_FD_TO_HANDLE, ...) = 0                 renderD128, v3d
   ioctl(34, DRM_IOCTL_PRIME_FD_TO_HANDLE, ...) = -1 EINVAL         card0, vc4
 .
 The EINVAL becomes "nullptr returned from gbm_bo_import", then
 "CreateSharedImage: could not create backing", and the window has no content at
 all. Note the minigbm half of that chain is only in /var/log/ui/ui.LATEST, not
 /var/log/chrome/chrome. On a normal board card0 *is* the GPU, so this never
 appears; rpi5 is immune for the same reason 0017 excludes it, BCM2712 puts
 the display behind an IOMMU.
 .
 Being contiguous is not enough on its own. With 0014 the buffer is already
 CMA-backed -- CmaFree drops 22.7 MB per launch -- and vc4 still refuses it,
 because gralloc exports the *v3d GEM object* wrapping those pages rather than
 the heap dma-buf: /sys/kernel/debug/dma_buf/bufinfo shows exp_name "drm" with
 v3d_render fences and never "linux,cma". v3d_bo_export already hands out the
 heap fd, but only for a BO that took the heap path, and after 0017 a window
 buffer no longer does.
 .
 So mark the buffers that actually leave the container instead of widening the
 contiguous set again. SurfaceFlinger's TaskRenderSurface -- the only allocator
 of buffers fydroid hands to Chrome -- sets a vendor usage bit that arrives here
 as BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT, and v3d treats it as a hard requirement: it must
 come from the CMA heap, so v3d_bo_export gives Chrome the heap fd, which vc4 can
 import. Everything else keeps 0017's placement, so the pool pays only for what
 is displayed.
 .
 The flag must NOT take part in combination matching. drv_get_combination()
 requires a combination's mask to be a superset of the requested flags, and
 TaskRenderSurface sets this bit on every board -- advertising it only in v3d's
 table would make the lookup miss on amdgpu, virtgpu_virgl, rockchip, realtek and
 vmwgfx, and gralloc would reject every ARC window buffer as UNSUPPORTED. Nor can
 it be gated per board: fydroid-rt_arm64 compiles rockchip+v3d+vc4+realtek into
 one image and picks at runtime. It is therefore declared a placement hint and
 stripped at the top of drv_get_combination, the same shape as the existing
 BO_USE_TEST_ALLOC strip; drv_bo_create still passes the full flags to
 backend->bo_create, so v3d sees it and every other backend never does.
 .
 The bit is 1ULL<<55, inside BufferUsage::VENDOR_MASK_HI, deliberately not
 GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_0: bit 28 is already BUFFER_USAGE_FRONT_RENDERING_PRIVATE
 in cros_gralloc_helpers.h and is handled earlier in cros_gralloc_convert_usage,
 which silently converts it to BO_USE_FRONT_RENDERING instead.
 .
 Pairs with the TaskRenderSurface change in
 fydroid-rt-common/frameworks/native/services/surfaceflinger. The two must ship
 together: a new SurfaceFlinger against an old gralloc hits "Unhandled gralloc
 usage", which returns BO_USE_NONE and fails every ARC buffer allocation.
 .
 Verified on rpi4-openfyde, v3d, 1080p and 3840x2160: F-Droid renders,
 gbm_bo_import failures 1044 -> 0, PRIME_FD_TO_HANDLE failures 1046 -> 0, and
 dma-bufs now export as "linux,cma" where there were none. At 4K fullscreen the
 pool allocates 3840x2304 buffers with 0 cma_alloc and 0 GraphicBufferAllocator
 failures -- the original 4K failure signature -- holding 105.8 MiB of heap dma-bufs,
 and cold-boot CmaFree is 282648 kB, in line with the 286004 kB 0017 measured.
 Composed-frame throttling fell from 50-58% to 4-17% now that Chrome can import
 and release. No regression on fydroid_rt_apple (vmwgfx) or
 fydroid_rt_arm64 (rockchip/panthor): both render with 0 allocation
 failures, 0 "Unhandled gralloc usage" and 0 "No combo found". Builds clean for
 armv8, arm64, apple and amd64.
diff --git a/drv.h b/drv.h
index 38ee79f..a112ad9 100644
--- a/drv.h
+++ b/drv.h
@@ -43,6 +43,23 @@ extern "C" {
 #define BO_USE_GPU_DATA_BUFFER		(1ull << 18)
 #define BO_USE_SENSOR_DIRECT_DATA	(1ull << 19)
 
+/*
+ * fydroid-private: this buffer is exported as a dma-buf and imported by the
+ * Chrome OS compositor. On a Pi that import lands on vc4 (card0), which has no
+ * IOMMU, so the buffer has to be CMA-backed *and* handed over as the CMA
+ * dma-heap fd -- see V3D_CONTIGUOUS_REQUIRED in v3d.c.
+ */
+#define BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT	(1ull << 62)
+
+/*
+ * Placement hints: they tell a backend WHERE to put a buffer, not what layouts
+ * it can produce, so they must not take part in combination matching.
+ * drv_get_combination() requires a combination's mask to be a superset of the
+ * requested flags, and no backend advertises these -- leaving one in the match
+ * would fail every allocation carrying it, on every backend that does not know
+ * it, as UNSUPPORTED.
+ */
+#define BO_USE_PLACEMENT_HINT_MASK	(BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT)
 #define BO_USE_ARC_SCREEN_CAP_PROBED	(1ull << 63)
 
 /* Quirks for allocating a buffer. */
diff --git a/drv.c b/drv.c
index fff26df..9ca9cfb 100644
--- a/drv.c
+++ b/drv.c
@@ -223,6 +223,9 @@ struct combination *drv_get_combination(struct driver *drv, uint32_t format, uin
 {
 	struct combination *curr, *best;
 
+	/* Placement hints are not format capabilities -- see drv.h. */
+	use_flags &= ~BO_USE_PLACEMENT_HINT_MASK;
+
 	if (format == DRM_FORMAT_NONE || use_flags == BO_USE_NONE)
 		return 0;
 
diff --git a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_helpers.cc b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_helpers.cc
index 2b3decf..6d78c66 100644
--- a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_helpers.cc
+++ b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_helpers.cc
@@ -18,6 +18,19 @@
 /* Define to match AIDL BufferUsage::GPU_DATA_BUFFER. */
 #define BUFFER_USAGE_GPU_DATA_BUFFER (1 << 24)
 
+/*
+ * fydroid-private: set by TaskRenderSurface on the per-task composition buffers,
+ * the only buffers fydroid exports to Chrome. Must be consumed here -- an
+ * unhandled usage bit fails the whole conversion.
+ *
+ * Lives in BufferUsage::VENDOR_MASK_HI (bits 48-63), NOT in the low vendor
+ * nibble: GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_0 (bit 28) is already spoken for by
+ * BUFFER_USAGE_FRONT_RENDERING_PRIVATE in cros_gralloc_helpers.h, and since it
+ * is handled earlier in cros_gralloc_convert_usage it silently swallows the bit
+ * and yields BO_USE_FRONT_RENDERING instead.
+ */
+#define BUFFER_USAGE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT (1ULL << 55)
+
 /* Define to match AIDL PixelFormat::R_8. */
 #define HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_R8 0x38
 
@@ -148,6 +161,8 @@ uint64_t cros_gralloc_convert_usage(uint64_t usage)
 	handle_usage(&usage, BUFFER_USAGE_FRONT_RENDERING, &use_flags, BO_USE_FRONT_RENDERING);
 	handle_usage(&usage, BUFFER_USAGE_FRONT_RENDERING_PRIVATE, &use_flags,
 		     BO_USE_FRONT_RENDERING);
+	handle_usage(&usage, BUFFER_USAGE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT, &use_flags,
+		     BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT);
 
 	if (usage) {
 		ALOGE("Unhandled gralloc usage: %llx", (unsigned long long)usage);
diff --git a/v3d.c b/v3d.c
index 980c125..115975d 100644
--- a/v3d.c
+++ b/v3d.c
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@
  */
 #define V3D_CONTIGUOUS_REQUIRED                                                                    \
 	(BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER | BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER | BO_USE_CAMERA_READ |                   \
-	 BO_USE_CAMERA_WRITE | BO_USE_SENSOR_DIRECT_DATA)
+	 BO_USE_CAMERA_WRITE | BO_USE_SENSOR_DIRECT_DATA | BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT)
 
 /*
  * The display/cursor half: buffers a KMS plane would scan out. These are a SOFT
@@ -78,8 +78,13 @@
  * a single image carries backends that do drive real scanout hardware and do
  * depend on BO_USE_SCANOUT. The decision has to stay backend-local, here.
  *
- * To restore the old behaviour (e.g. if Chrome turns out to want ARC buffers on
- * a hardware overlay after all), give this the non-Android definition.
+ * Chrome does still need the buffers it actually displays to be CMA-backed --
+ * it imports them on vc4 (card0), which has no IOMMU on BCM2711 and refuses a
+ * pageable v3d BO with EINVAL. That is handled precisely rather than by putting
+ * SCANOUT back here: SurfaceFlinger marks its per-task composition buffers with
+ * BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT, which is in V3D_CONTIGUOUS_REQUIRED above. Those
+ * are the only buffers that leave the container, so the pool pays for them and
+ * nothing else.
  */
 #ifdef __ANDROID__
 #define V3D_CONTIGUOUS_SOFT 0
@@ -98,7 +103,8 @@
  */
 #define V3D_LINEAR_USE                                                                             \
 	(BO_USE_NON_GPU_HW | BO_USE_CURSOR | BO_USE_SW_MASK | BO_USE_LINEAR |                       \
-	 BO_USE_GPU_DATA_BUFFER | BO_USE_RENDERSCRIPT | BO_USE_PROTECTED)
+	 BO_USE_GPU_DATA_BUFFER | BO_USE_RENDERSCRIPT | BO_USE_PROTECTED |                          \
+	 BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT)
 
 enum v3d_tiling_mode {
         /* Untiled resources.  Not valid as texture inputs. */
@@ -380,6 +386,20 @@ static int v3d_bo_create(struct bo *bo, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_
    * ARC_CALLOC makes v3d borrow the BO from vc4's CMA allocator; without it the
    * BO is ordinary pageable memory behind the v3d MMU.
    */
+  /*
+   * A BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT buffer that does not come from the heap is not
+   * merely slower, it is useless: the vc4 borrow below is contiguous but is
+   * exported as a v3d GEM handle, and Chrome imports these on vc4 (card0),
+   * which refuses a re-exported v3d object with EINVAL. The allocation then
+   * succeeds and the window renders nothing, with no error anywhere -- exactly
+   * the failure this flag exists to prevent. Say so.
+   */
+  if (use_flags & BO_USE_ARC_COMPOSER_EXPORT)
+    drv_loge("v3d: composer-export buffer %ux%u has no CMA dma-heap to come from "
+             "(heap_fd=%d); Chrome will not be able to import it and the window "
+             "will be blank\n",
+             width, height, dpriv ? dpriv->heap_fd : -1);
+
   bo_create.size = bo->meta.total_size;
   bo_create.flags = contiguous ? ARC_CALLOC : 0;
   if (contiguous || linear) {
